    story: ["Three young men stand before the most powerful king on earth, with the furnace already roaring behind them, and they will not bow.", "Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego do not bargain. They state what they believe: the God they serve is able to rescue them. The next verse goes further, saying that even if He does not, they will still refuse the golden image. Their confidence rests in who God is, not in a guaranteed result. The story shows a fourth figure walking in the fire with them, and Nebuchadnezzar ends by blessing the God he meant to defy.", "Whatever you are facing, trust that He is able. Hold to Him, whether or not it ends the way you hope."],
